The location of the Kloset store the `plakar` binary of the node writes the
snapshots to.

A local path uses the `fs` storage built in the `plakar` binary. A
`sftp://` or `s3://` location requires the `sftp` or `s3` plakar package to
be installed on every node, with `plakar pkg add`, in the package directory
the driver passes with `-datadir`.

A store must never be included in a backed up resource.
